<title>USA: Pinellas Cty, Fla., to vote on sales tax extension.</title>
<headline>Pinellas Cty, Fla., to vote on sales tax extension.</headline>
<dateline>CLEARWATER, Fla. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters in Florida's Pinellas County are scheduled to vote Tuesday on a proposal to extend a one-cent sales tax for road, park, drainage and other infrastructure projects.</p>
<p>If extended for another 10 years, the &quot;Penny for Pinellas&quot; tax would raise $1.4 billion to be divided amoung the county and its 24 municipalities.</p>
<p>The local-option sales tax was adopted in 1989 by a margin of only 398 votes. If voters reject the extension, the tax would expire in 2000 and the county's sales tax rate would drop to six percent from seven percent.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
